  "slug": "embedding-kernels-function-relationships-30bc",
  "summary": "Five preprints apply long-read, methylation and k-mer methods to somatic mutation, mutation spectra, centromeres and benchmarking of difficult genomic regions.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is quantifying genomic variation where short-read or reference-based approaches are limited. PacBio HiFi sequencing gives cortical neuron point mutation rates of about 25.9 per diploid genome per year, similar in mice and humans. Context-dependent mutation spectra, with GC-biased gene conversion, are used to model equilibrium trinucleotide composition across 25 plants and 10 mammals. Pooch assigns parent of origin to Hi-C-phased diploid assemblies from differentially methylated CpGs, and cenlen estimates centromere array lengths from short reads in 2,557 1000 Genomes individuals. A stratified HG002 benchmark shows short-read deficits in low-mappability and duplicated regions. New relative to prior material: the focus shifts to centromeres, haplotype assignment and region-stratified accuracy.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
